<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n82891" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πηγός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, 
			Dor.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πᾱγός</span></b> , (<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πήγνυμι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					11
				</span></i>
			) <i>well put together, solid, strong</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἵππους πηγοὺς ἀθλοφόρους</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					9.124
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Alcm.
				23.48
			</span></i> ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κύματι πηγῷ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					5.388
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				23.235
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				9.143
			</span></i> (Antip.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			Subst.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πηγός</span> (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἅλς</span>), ὁ, <i>salt</i>
			(cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πηκτός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					111
				</span></i>
			), mock-Epic use in <i><span class="en">
				Strato Com.
				1.36
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>white</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πλόκος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Lyc.
					336
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀστέα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Sammelb.</u>
					4314.5
				</span></i>
			 (Alexandria, <span class="entity">iii B. C.</span>); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κύνας ἥμισυ πηγούς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Call.
					<u>Dian.</u>
					90
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i> has <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πηγόν: οἱ μὲν λευκόν, οἱ δὲ
				μέλαν</span>; and <i><span class="en">
				Eust.
				403.43
			</span></i> explains <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κῦμα π.</span> as
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κ. μέλαν</span>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				740.50
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				1539.42
			</span></i>.</div>
